{"task_id": "HumanEval/40", "solution": "def triples_sum_to_zero(l: list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Main algorithm entry point that finds zero-sum triples.\n    Returns True if three distinct elements sum to zero, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _validate_input_size(l_inner: list):\n        \"\"\"Helper function to check minimum size requirement.\"\"\"\n        return len(l_inner) >= 3\n\n    def _generate_combinations(l_inner: list):\n        \"\"\"Generator for distinct triple combinations (indices).\"\"\"\n        n = len(l_inner)\n        for i in range(n):\n            for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                for k in range(j + 1, n):\n                    yield (i, j, k)\n\n    def _calculate_sum(triple_indices: tuple, l_inner: list):\n        \"\"\"Calculate sum for given triple indices.\"\"\"\n        return l_inner[triple_indices[0]] + l_inner[triple_indices[1]] + l_inner[triple_indices[2]]\n\n    if not _validate_input_size(l):\n        return False\n\n    for indices_triple in _generate_combinations(l):\n        if _calculate_sum(indices_triple, l) == 0:\n            return True\n\n    return False"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/42", "solution": "def incr_list(l: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Return a new list with each element incremented by 1.\n    This function processes numeric lists while preserving order and immutability.\n    >>> incr_list([1, 2, 3])\n    [2, 3, 4]\n    >>> incr_list([5, 3, 5, 2, 3, 3, 9, 0, 123])\n    [6, 4, 6, 3, 4, 4, 10, 1, 124]\n    >>> incr_list([])\n    []\n    >>> incr_list([1.5, 2.5])\n    [2.5, 3.5]\n    \"\"\"\n    return [x + 1 for x in l]"}
