{"task_id": "HumanEval/59", "solution": "def _find_prime_factors(n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Finds all prime factors of a composite integer n.\n    This function iteratively divides n by factors starting from 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    factors = []\n    d = 2\n    temp_n = n\n    while d * d <= temp_n:\n        while temp_n % d == 0:\n            factors.append(d)\n            temp_n //= d\n        d += 1\n    if temp_n > 1:\n        factors.append(temp_n)\n    return factors\ndef largest_prime_factor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return the largest prime factor of n. Assume n > 1 and is not a prime.\n\n    Args:\n        n (int): Composite integer greater than 1\n\n    Returns:\n        int: The largest prime factor of n\n\n    Examples:\n        >>> largest_prime_factor(13195)\n        29\n        >>> largest_prime_factor(2048)\n        2\n    \"\"\"\n    # Find all prime factors of the input number.\n    prime_factors = _find_prime_factors(n)\n    # Return the maximum prime factor from the list.\n    return max(prime_factors)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/59", "solution": "def largest_prime_factor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return the largest prime factor of n. Assume n > 1 and is not a prime.\n    >>> largest_prime_factor(13195)\n    29\n    >>> largest_prime_factor(2048)\n    2\n    \"\"\"\n    last_factor = 1\n\n    # Divide by 2 until n is odd\n    while n % 2 == 0:\n        last_factor = 2\n        n //= 2\n\n    # Check for odd factors starting from 3\n    i = 3\n    while i * i <= n:\n        while n % i == 0:\n            last_factor = i\n            n //= i\n        i += 2 # Only check odd numbers\n\n    # If n is still greater than 1, it must be the largest prime factor\n    if n > 1:\n        last_factor = n\n\n    return last_factor"}
